  "body": "## What changed\n\nSix tests made a GPU device without `gpu_guard`. They now take the guard as their first statement.\n\n- `crates/ui/tests/egui_app.rs`:\n  - `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`\n  - `a_headless_start_with_a_model_file_imports_and_draws_it`\n  - `a_headless_start_with_a_project_file_opens_and_draws_it`\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs` (ignored pixel snapshots):\n  - `egui_shell_snapshot`\n  - `egui_shell_snapshot_light`\n  - `tool_editor_snapshot`\n\nThe change uses the existing `headless_gpu::gpu_guard()`. It adds no lock type. It does not change the thread count. It changes test code only.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe three headless tests run `camcraft_ui::run` in parallel. Each run reaches `headless_gpu::device()`. The tests made and dropped wgpu devices at the same time. #3589 and #3605 show that this ends the process on Windows.\n\nThe snapshot tests make the egui_kittest renderer. They are ignored, so they run only in the release lane.\n\n## Search\n\nI searched `crates/ui/src` for these items: wgpu instance, adapter and device calls, `View3D::new`, headless runs, kittest `render` and `snapshot` calls, and the screenshot command. I read `tests/egui_app.rs`. I found no other unguarded GPU test in the `egui_app` binary or the lib binary. I found no lib test that opens a window or a native dialog. The search read the source. It did not trace the processes.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, both in `egui_app::gpu_test_lock`:\n\n- `every_headless_run_of_the_egui_app_binary_takes_the_lock` (new). A new test in `egui_app.rs` must take the guard, or must be in the list of tests that make no device.\n- `every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock` (the table has three more entries).\n\nRed before the fix: yes. Both pins failed on the unchanged test files:\n\n```\ntests.rs: fn egui_shell_snapshot() must start with `let _gpu = gpu_guard();` or take `test_gpu`, found \"let _g = snapshot_guard();\"\ntests/egui_app.rs: start with `let _gpu = ...gpu_guard();`, or list a test that makes no device: [\"egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero\", \"a_headless_start_with_a_model_file_imports_and_draws_it\", \"a_headless_start_with_a_project_file_opens_and_draws_it\"]\n```\n\nMutation check: I removed each of the six guards, one at a time. The pins were red each time. They were green after the restore.\n\nResults on the final head, on macOS:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 11 steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work`: 45 passed, 4 ignored (heavy lane).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib snapshot -- --ignored`: the three tests ran to the end with no deadlock. All three failed the pixel comparison on this machine. I did not run them without the guards, so I do not have a baseline. This PR changes no snapshot PNG.\n\nHeavy lanes: not run. The diff does not touch motion, sim, post, geometry or app operations.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The catalog suites above passed, apart from the 4 ignored tests. The diff changes no recorded program.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows. I cannot reach the Windows machines. I did not reproduce the crash.\n- The M5 coordinator runs the Windows repro on `lenny` and `bacon`. Please wait for that result before the merge, because the merge closes #3379.\n- `tests/gpu_render.rs` uses its own lock. I did not audit that binary.\n- `tests/shell.rs` and `tests/catalog_render.rs` have one device test each. This PR does not change them.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#3922, #3832 and #3103 touch `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`. They touch the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Tests: the last unguarded GPU tests of the UI `egui_app` and lib binaries now run one at a time.\n\nFixes #3379\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
